{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing","id":1163625,"title":"Is Temporal Dislocation still a thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-29T11:23:05-08:00","id":1163625,"title":"Is Temporal Dislocation still a thing?","content":"One element of 1e's Durances that I found fascinating was that the time spent by the changeling in Faerie didn't necessarily match up with the time that passed on Earth: a changeling could spend months, years, or even decades trapped in Faerie only to escape and find that only a single night passed back home; or a changeling might be trapped in Faerie for mere days only to find that months, years, or even decades have passed since they disappeared. Taken to extremes, this can lead to a fairly unique kind of alienation \u2014 in particular, a short Durance disjointed from a long absence on Earth can lead to an anachronistic changeling. I built a 1e character around this notion: a mid-30s changeling whose estranged daughter is now the same age as her and whose fetch is an elderly socialite who basically runs the town. <br /> <br /> Does 2e still support this notion, or did the temporal dislocation thing end up falling through the cracks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T11:41:01-08:00","id":1163632,"title":"","content":"It is! And it sounds like the hard limits have been removed. One of the npcs of Ipswich sounds like they returned hundreds of years later. This is unlike 1e, where I think the max was a century. I'm glad for this change, as well the extended lifespan. It really fits the feel of a fairy tale. <br /> <br /> As memories are what draw you home, there are likely SOME limits. If absolutely nothing you knew in life exists even slightly in the mortal world anymore, it's likely you won't get any further than the Hedge, and end up a hobgoblin. But back, such a circumstance is literally unimaginable, because if someone could think of it, it hasn't been forgotten, and thus could still serve as a beacon.<br /> <br /> Good luck with it though, you might stumble into some random kid's bedroom, bleeding, terrified, and terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T11:42:41-08:00","id":1163635,"title":"","content":"Yup, it's still a thing in 2E, in both ways. Mentions are made of the challenges displaced Changelings face in the Kickstarter Backer preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:03:58-08:00","id":1163664,"title":"","content":"Ok. Now, does it ever go backward? That is, does a changeling ever escape to a time <i>before</i> she was taken? I can see why a Storyteller might want to avoid the headaches of a time loop; so I'm guessing that if it happens it's rare. But what about, say, a historian who is deeply familiar with a particular past era, gets abducted from modern-day New York, and escapes to the world of Lilly, Saber, and Thorn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T13:08:29-08:00","id":1163667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1163664#post1163664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Now, does it ever go backward? That is, does a changeling ever escape to a time <i>before</i> she was taken? I can see why a Storyteller might want to avoid the headaches of a time loop; so I'm guessing that if it happens it's rare. But what about, say, a historian who is deeply familiar with a particular past era, gets abducted from modern-day New York, and escapes to the world of Lilly, Saber, and Thorn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? That's basically the plot of Outlander with slight modification and that series is deeply appropriate for Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a>