00","id":1163676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1163671#post1163671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of Outlander. Gonna have to do something about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the gore and sex of Game of Thrones, with an extra side of romance and time travel between WWII and the Jacobite Risings. Very highly recommended. If I were to do a Dark Era of it, it would either be Changeling/Demon or straight up Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T07:20:54-08:00","id":1167602,"title":"","content":"Ok, this looks like the best place to raise a question of mine: if a mage instills an anchor to prevent a person from traveling in time (let's ignore &quot;how&quot; for the moment), and they spend time in Faerie, is this &quot;anchor&quot; likely to be a factor in how much or little time has transpired when they return?<br /> <br /> In other words, do mage Time effects trump the inherent magic of Faerie?<br /> <br /> Confession: my knowledge of Changeling is about thimble-deep, but there CofD's version looks much more interesting, and I'm mildly excited by the potential of 2e and fae-touched in particular.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T07:42:19-08:00","id":1167606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1167602#post1167602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, this looks like the best place to raise a question of mine: if a mage instills an anchor to prevent a person from traveling in time (let's ignore &quot;how&quot; for the moment), and they spend time in Faerie, is this &quot;anchor&quot; likely to be a factor in how much or little time has transpired when they return?<br /> <br /> In other words, do mage Time effects trump the inherent magic of Faerie?<br /> <br /> Confession: my knowledge of Changeling is about thimble-deep, but there CofD's version looks much more interesting, and I'm mildly excited by the potential of 2e and fae-touched in particular.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmages themselves, even the Exarchs themselves, haven't figured out how to stop the shenanigans of the Gentry, even after editing them out of the Tapestry and trying to quarantine them in the supernal Arcadia. The True Far are quite up there in terms of power, and a regular mage had better study how his magic will interact with the oaths and contracts of the Kindly Ones.<br /> <br /> That being said, unless this time anchor thing DIRECTLY affects the storylife/legend of a given true fae, it is unlikely they would care. Let the mage TRY to control time, if he's bold enough, for all They care. They'll only notice if his spell ruins their slow motion dramatic entrance, or if it helps a slave realize they have NOT toiled for mortal lifetimes. The supernal truths of Faerie are very different than Ironside, however, so how likely a Mage is to form an effective imago without it unravelling into Paradox.. thats an iffy question, but really, it comes down to the mood of the Wyrd or the nearest Gentry (or unshaped Huntsmen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  Autocorrect, my foulest foe and greatest crutch 12-14-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:46:39-08:00","id":1167653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1167606#post1167606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Archmages themselves, even the Exarchs themselves, haven't figured out how to stop the shenanigans of the Gentry, even after editing them out of the Tapestry and trying to quarantine them in the supernal Arcadia. The True Far are quite up there in terms of power, and a regular mage had better study how his magic will interact with the oaths and contracts of the Kindly Ones.<br /> <br /> That being said, unless this time anchor thing DIRECTLY affects the storylife/legend of a given true fae, it is unlikely they would care. Let the mage TRY to control time, if he's bold enough, for all They care. They'll only notice if his spell ruins their slow motion dramatic entrance, or if it helps a slave realize they have NOT toiled for mortal lifetimes. The supernal truths of Faerie are very different than Ironside, however, so how likely a Mage is to form an effective imago without it unravelling into Paradox.. thats an iffy question, but really, it comes down to the mood of the Wyrd or the nearest Gentry (or unshaped Huntsmen).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you--this is both concise and useful on many fronts. As I understand it then any attempts to constrain or &quot;nudge&quot; Faerie with regards to time (or, whatever else) is subject to True Fae veto, but they may not care if it isn't something core to their name.<br /> <br /> Since you are, indeed, the Cleverest of Things, let me lay out a quick scenario that I am intending to result in a Fae-Touched, but not a Changeling. My story is set in Arthurian Britain, so some Faerie crossover is pretty much required, but I have to keep the touch rules-light or abstracted, lest I become overwhelmed....<br /> <br /> * PC offends the Queen of the Black Thorn and, within the hedge chasing a child she promised to protect, is subjected to a curse that would turn her into one of the Fae's slave thorn-warriors. She escapes the hedge but is delivered to a rival Fae (yes, the Queen of the White Thorn, among other Names) who &quot;fixes&quot; the problem to a level of satisfaction and then permits PC to leave after a while. (Because, rival Fae, as well as Promises.)<br /> <br /> * PC gets a Seeming and, if printed merits support it, wooden skin. Hilarity ensues.<br /> <br /> You've fixed one problem I had with PC, in that she had some protection from temporal dislocation (long story). I get to reasonably ignore that. Yay!<br /> <br /> Am I barking up the wrong thornbush with the end-result of this scenario?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T04:38:04-08:00","id":1167867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1163676#post1163676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the gore and sex of Game of Thrones, with an extra side of romance and time travel between WWII and the Jacobite Risings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has a nice touch in that the time traveller is from shortly after WWII, where she was a battlefield nurse. Which means <i>she's</i> the one who's seen war and death on a scale the <i>Jacobites</i> can't fathom, which is good for Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T07:48:09-08:00","id":1167912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1167653#post1167653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you--this is both concise and useful on many fronts. As I understand it then any attempts to constrain or &amp;quot;nudge&amp;quot; Faerie with regards to time (or, whatever else) is subject to True Fae veto, but they may not care if it isn't something core to their name.<br /> <br /> Since you are, indeed, the Cleverest of Things, let me lay out a quick scenario that I am intending to result in a Fae-Touched, but not a Changeling. My story is set in Arthurian Britain, so some Faerie crossover is pretty much required, but I have to keep the touch rules-light or abstracted, lest I become overwhelmed....<br /> <br /> * PC offends the Queen of the Black Thorn and, within the hedge chasing a child she promised to protect, is subjected to a curse that would turn her into one of the Fae's slave thorn-warriors. She escapes the hedge but is delivered to a rival Fae (yes, the Queen of the White Thorn, among other Names) who &amp;quot;fixes&amp;quot; the problem to a level of satisfaction and then permits PC to leave after a while. (Because, rival Fae, as well as Promises.)<br /> <br /> * PC gets a Seeming and, if printed merits support it, wooden skin. Hilarity ensues.<br /> <br /> You've fixed one problem I had with PC, in that she had some protection from temporal dislocation (long story). I get to reasonably ignore that. Yay!<br /> <br /> Am I barking up the wrong thornbush with the end-result of this scenario?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>The PC is a mage? Hmmm... I suppose it might work, becoming fae-touched in a weird way, though with obvious restrictions on certain traits that are too tied to the splat. <br /> <br /> Now, a very interesting question is... what did Faerie get out of the deal? Everything comes with a cost, and for a Mage, goodness knows what noticed and decided to buy up. Whilst the twin Thorns are the immediate part of that, it goes down to what she promised the Thorn Queens librarian so that the pc might try to grasp a sane imago in that mad place, all the way up to what the Wyrd took away when it put some strangeness in its place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T08:57:12-08:00","id":1167927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163625-is-temporal-dislocation-still-a-thing?p=1167912#post1167912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The PC is a mage? Hmmm... I suppose it might work, becoming fae-touched in a weird way, though with obvious restrictions on certain traits that are too tied to the splat.<br /> <br /> Now, a very interesting question is... what did Faerie get out of the deal? Everything comes with a cost, and for a Mage, goodness knows what noticed and decided to buy up. Whilst the twin Thorns are the immediate part of that, it goes down to what she promised the Thorn Queens librarian so that the pc might try to grasp a sane imago in that mad place, all the way up to what the Wyrd took away when it put some strangeness in its place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fortunately PC is not a mage, and is purposefully avoiding major splats for as long as is fun in the story. The Time-related spell is a hanging effect by [something] else to prevent involuntary temporal travel-muckery; and frankly it's no longer needed for story purposes, so if a True Fae unravels it that's cool. On the other hand it also gives an excuse to NOT cause the PC to lose much time while in Faerie accumulating disturbing flashback material. Thanks to your Cleverest answers I have confidence in this area. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To your Interesting-est of questions: I'm still working that out. The aspect of Faerie that everything is transactional rather than moral is, to me, a very interesting counterpoint to the moral quandaries of the mortal world. After all you do NOT thank a faerie creature for helping you out--they did so because either instructions flowed down from superiors, or there was some other quid-pro-quo at work, implicit or explicit!<br /> <br /> Here's a few ideas: Faerie as a whole gets the PC's service 9 times (9 being a mystically significant number of transformation, see Odin 9 days hanging, 9 years a wolf for Lyacon, etc.), and they are expressly sucked into the British-Isles play of seelie/unseelie courts and periodic battles. This is an Arthurian backdrop after all. The incident may also cost PC their firstborn, which may go unnoticed and who may return later as a real changeling... there are things that are lost in the bargaining with Faerie, and memory of everything agreed can be one of them. It's also possible that the obligations to Faerie may get bartered around to other fae lords.<br /> <br /> There may well be many more costs. PC will continue to carry Fae curses from the Queen of the Black Thorn until she dies (literally or metaphorically) in an gender-swapped expression of the story of Balin and Balan. If you're familiar with it, it pretty much sucks to be Balin.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}